---
description: Always use plural names for API resources and feature routes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Plural Naming (mandatory)

Resource names are **always plural**, never singular.

## HTTP routes

```typescript
@Controller('users')        // ✅
@Controller('categories')   // ✅
@Controller('products')     // ✅

@Controller('user')         // ❌
@Controller('category')     // ❌
@Controller('product')      // ❌
```

## Also plural

- Module folders for collections: prefer plural when creating new resources (`products/`, `orders/`)
- Paginated result keys: `buildPaginatedResult('users', …)` / `'categories'` — plural collection name
- URL path segments for list/CRUD resources under `/api/...`

## Allowed singular (non-collection)

These are actions/areas, not resource collections:

- `auth` (signup/signin/…)
- `profile` (current user self-service)

## When adding a feature

1. Pick a plural English noun for the route
2. Use that same plural in `@Controller('…')`
3. Never introduce a new singular CRUD route
